{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Stay here with the donkey.</b> Midrash: When Avraham saw the place from afar and a cloud bound upon it, he said to Yitzchak his son: What do you see? He said to him: A fine mountain with a cloud bound upon it. He turned to his young men and said to them: What do you see? They said to him: We do not see anything. He said to them: You are equal to the donkey, for you do not see as it does; if so, ״שבו לכם פה עם החמור״ — stay here with the donkey. And it seems to me that this is that which the Rabbis, blessed be their memory, said: ״עם הדומה לחמור״ — like one who is comparable to a donkey; and therefore a slave has no share in the World-to-Come, like a donkey."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:05:47.107710188Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}